  "id": "COMPOUND:22758 - PROTEIN:5702",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex, multi-step relationship between CID 3002104 and CCF-STTG1, with CID 3002104 acting as a target for multiple compounds that ultimately target CCF-STTG1. The core mechanism appears to involve the interaction of CID 3002104 with various chemical entities, which are all linked to CCF-STTG1 through a series of target relationships. These compounds, including (7E,9E,16Z)-18-hydroxyoctadeca-7,9,16-trien-11,13-diyn-4-one and (1R,2R,4S,7Z,11R)-4,8-dimethyl-12-methylidene-3,14-dioxatricyclo[9.3.0.02,4]tetradec-7-en-13-one, are all structurally distinct but share a common pathway of interaction with VMRC-LCP, which in turn targets CCF-STTG1. The evidence supports a mechanism where CID 3002104 is a central node in a network of compounds that ultimately interact with CCF-STTG1 through a series of intermediate targets. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of VMRC-LCP as a key mediator in the relationship between CID 3002104 and CCF-STTG1, with the compounds acting as diverse but related ligands that converge on this central target.",
